Green. `625 total, 625 passing, 0 failing`, exit 0.

Only 3 of the 625 cases were actually broken. All three were in `order totals`, and all had a discount and a tax at the same time. `orderTotal` in `src/pricing.js` took the discount off correctly, then charged tax on the original price instead of the discounted one. The rest of the wall of text was passing cases and a coverage table.

The fix, one line:

```js
function orderTotal(cents, discountPct, taxRate) {
  const discounted = applyDiscount(cents, discountPct);
  return applyTax(discounted, taxRate);
}
```

The function's own comment already described this behavior, so the code was the thing that was wrong, not the tests.
